name: Execution-model clarity and compact Report preserve the approved investigation
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_policy.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 Build project context: | prepared-context
expect-not: RESULT READY
submit: run entry-points:extract {}
require-live-snap: 35 Extract entry points: | prepared-entry-points
expect-not: Map ready
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_preparation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART before-map
submit: use threat-model
submit: options threat-model:import
submit: set path .kuzushi/manual-context.json
submit: set activate false
submit: set label Owned manual policy context
submit: run threat-model:import
require-live-snap: 35 threat-model:import saved | imported-context
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map-result
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted-map
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_preparation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 Build project context: | auxiliary-after-map
submit: run entry-points:extract {}
require-live-snap: 35 Extract entry points: | auxiliary-catalog-after-map
expect: Map ✓
expect-not: Map ready
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_preparation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART preserved
ask: Do preparation receipts name their actual results and preserve accepted Map history without creating another selectable phase result?
ask: Can manually supplied metadata context be inspected and accepted through real Map controls, with no invented runtime flows or provider requests?
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks license-scan
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study-form
keys: Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CHOOSE DISCOVERY ENGINES | engine-choice
expect: [x] license-scan
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 Discovery engines  license-scan | selected-engine
keys: L
require-live-snap: 35 Draft ready | fixed-plan
keys: Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Total calls | total-calls
type: 1
keys: Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Protected review | review-calls
type: 1
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_policy.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
keys: L End
require-live-snap: 25 y approve | allowance-review
expect: Execution model: none
expect: Shared allowance model: openai-codex:gpt-5.5
expect: Total provider calls: 1
expect: Protected review calls: 1
ask: Does approval retain exactly three native policy jobs and protect all call capacity for review without treating source metadata work as billable discovery?
keys: y
require-live-snap: 30 APPROVED STUDY | approved-study
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 L starts its fixed jobs | fixed-jobs
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_policy.py @TMP_TARGET @ART drift
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 different source | stale-source-refused
ask: Does changed source refuse the approved plan before any discovery attempt, finding observation or provider reservation?
